// specs.memql
//
// Common-namespace specs. Under the spec/shape binding redesign (epic
// #2281) a caller / authorization predicate is a `spec` bound to an
// @actor shape in its signature; it reads the projected envelope key by
// bare name and evaluates in-process (context-spec). Callers invoke it
// via spec("name") (e.g. the per-row-authz admin gate), never by bare
// name in a query filter.

/// Actor must hold an identity-issued JWT with the admin role.
spec actorEnvelope requiresAdmin {
  return role == "admin"
}

/// Caller must hold the owner or admin role.
///
/// Moved here from dsl/deployment/specs.memql in memql#2800: it is a generic
/// role predicate, not a deployment concept, and identity needs it to gate the
/// full-PII user read. It was defined-but-unused there (referenced only in
/// comments), so nothing changed behaviourally in the move.
///
/// Originally the legacy Deployment Console gate (#728): DeployStaging /
/// Promote / Rollback / RolloutAction / GetDeploymentStatus.
spec actorEnvelope requiresOwnerOrAdmin {
  return role == "admin" || role == "owner"
}
